From: Brad Barnett <127794626+bdbarnett@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 16:30:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] ncm_device: an out divisor Windows takes.

Windows' NCM driver (UsbNcm) refuses an out divisor of 1 or 2 and reports
the device as failed (Code 10) right after reading GET_NTB_PARAMETERS. It
starts on 4 or 8; Linux' cdc_ncm takes any of them.
---
 src/class/net/ncm_device.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/class/net/ncm_device.c b/src/class/net/ncm_device.c
--- a/src/class/net/ncm_device.c
+++ b/src/class/net/ncm_device.c
@@ -175,7 +175,9 @@
   .wNdbInAlignment          = TUD_NCM_ALIGNMENT,
   .wReserved                = 0,
   .dwNtbOutMaxSize          = CFG_TUD_NCM_OUT_NTB_MAX_SIZE,
-  .wNdbOutDivisor           = 1,
+  // Windows' NCM driver won't start on an out divisor of 1 or 2: it takes
+  // 4 or 8.
+  .wNdbOutDivisor           = 4,
   .wNdbOutPayloadRemainder  = 0,
   .wNdbOutAlignment         = TUD_NCM_ALIGNMENT,
   .wNtbOutMaxDatagrams      = CFG_TUD_NCM_OUT_MAX_DATAGRAMS_PER_NTB,
-- 
